# Pairs with AtomicAcrossCutover. The terminal is routed through the logical
# alias, so the retained redirect refuses it and it follows the alias to the
# shadow, where it installs the committed value of one key at a time.
MODULE: AtomicAcrossCutoverTerminalRoutedThroughAlias
TARGET: AtomicAcrossCutover
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a terminal the bound copy's redirect refuses is delivered to the alias copy
PERTURBS: Terminal

--- FIND
    /\ row' = IF dec = "committed" THEN [row EXCEPT ![bound][k] = New] ELSE row
    /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![bound][k] = FALSE]
    /\ term' = [term EXCEPT ![bound][k] = TRUE]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: a routed terminal follows the alias past a redirect.
    /\ LET tc == IF RoutedAdmits(bound) THEN bound ELSE alias IN
        /\ row' = IF dec = "committed" THEN [row EXCEPT ![tc][k] = New] ELSE row
        /\ pend' = [pend EXCEPT ![tc][k] = FALSE]
        /\ term' = [term EXCEPT ![tc][k] = TRUE]
--- END